<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">What lighting is code-required for industrial manufacturing?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Industrial facilities must meet OSHA and IESNA illumination standards, which typically require 30 to 100+ footcandles depending on the precision of the manufacturing task. High-visibility 5000K LED lighting is standard for safety and quality control.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">Are there DLC rebates for manufacturing plant retrofits?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Yes, manufacturing plants can secure substantial utility rebates by upgrading to DLC Premium high-bays and linear fixtures. Adding advanced lighting controls can often double the rebate amount.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__q">What IP ratings do industrial light fixtures need?</h3>
<p class="faq-item__a">Industrial environments with dust, debris, or moisture require IP65 or IP66 rated fixtures. Vapor tight fixtures and sealed high-bays prevent ingress and withstand high-pressure washdowns.</p>
</article>
